{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfQTXes8iuTR5FX2vPLAN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed on the current branch (not pushed, per instructions — the gates run after commit). Summary of the work:\n\n**Fixed three findings from item 214's spec:**\n\n1. **`attavo/verify.py`** — the \"returned\" record write site (forge checks not green) now computes and records the real `stub_ratio` instead of a hard-coded `None`. Moved the `approval_sha`/`spec_dir`/diff-since-approval computation earlier in `cmd_verify` so both the returned and pass write sites share it.\n2. **`attavo/build.py`** — the executor's environment now has `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` explicitly popped, so an inherited export from whoever launched `attavo build` can't resurrect the retired checks command inside the executor.\n3. **`.attavo/bin/select-tests`** — a deleted test file (`tests/test_*.py` that no longer exists) now falls through to the fail-safe whole-suite rule (`None` → `[\"tests\"]`) instead of silently selecting nothing.\n\nAdded the three named tests (`test_a_returned_review_carries_the_ratio_too`, `test_build_removes_inherited_attavo_checks_command_from_executor_environment`, `test_deleted_test_file_selects_the_whole_suite`) to `tests/test_stub_ratio.py` and `tests/test_testtool.py`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Both criteria shell scripts pass.\n- `python3 -m mypy attavo` exits 0, no `type: ignore`.\n- Full relevant test suite passes except one pre-existing test (`test_attavo_test_ends_a_run_past_its_bound_with_everything_it_started`) that fails only because this sandbox blocks `ps`/`os.killpg` outright — confirmed unrelated to my changes (untouched test, and `ps` fails standalone in this sandbox).\n- Finding #4 (builder recording a pass despite a failed type check) needed no change — confirmed closed by #212's gate, as the spec states.\n\nWork is committed on `attavo/214-four-findings`; not pushed."}],"container":null,